<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n106529" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑετ-ός</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῡ]</span>, ὁ, (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕὠ</span>”
				<i>rain,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					12.133
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				545
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποιεῖν ὑετόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>V.</u>
					263
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); esp. <i>a heavy shower</i> (whereas <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄμβρος</span> is continuous rain, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψεκάς</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψακάς</span> drizzle), <i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				5.22
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyn.</u>
				5.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mete.</u>
				347a12
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Mu.</u>
				394a31
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Chrysipp.Stoic.
				2.203
			</span></i>: pl., <i>rains,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Diog.
			</span></i> Apoll.<i><span class="en">
				3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>PA</u>
				653a4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as
				Adj. in 
				Sup.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνεμοι ὑετώτατοι</span> the
				<i>rainiest</i> winds, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.25
			</span></i> (where <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυετιώτατοι</span> cod. <i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑετιώτατοι</span> Hude). [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῡ</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
			</span></i>, 
				Att.
			; later <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ</span> in 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠετοῖο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Th.</u>
					273
				</span></i>
			.]</div>
